								<div class="title" id="post-title-1321758">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1019930&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608995930" alt="Anaxagoras" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1019930)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anaxagoras" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1019930); return false;" >Anaxagoras</a></span> <span class="odate time_1323154536 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2011 06:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1321758">
									

<p>This isn't my GoI, so I'm not exactly a final word on any of this, but here's how I see it.</p>
<p>The ancients actually did figure out where a whole bunch of nerves are located and what poking many of them does. The University-verse has long since taken this research and run with it. Initially as a punishment/reward system, then later as puppetry, then later as more subtle things. I kind of see them getting this stuff very quickly, and then remaining fairly stagnant for a long time. The teleportation thing is one of the few new technologies they have.</p>
<p>They're good at brain things, but most of the rest of their medical knowledge is terrible. They never abandon the teachings of the philosophers they deem &quot;great&quot;, even if they will distort them unintentionally. So, they believe in the humours thing, but also give far too much power to the brain. Obviously, the brain is important, but given a disease, they might conclude that it's caused by having too much bile, and give you a brain chip to make you hungry so you'll flush out all that bile.</p>
<p>Non-germ-based diseases, they're pretty good at. They can treat most psychological things, although unless they really respect you, they'd be more likely to just euthanize you, they're pretty good at surgery for tumors, that kind of thing, and their wound-healing technology is very fast, though lousy at preventing infection.</p>
<p>One thing I envision with Alexylva is a culture that values philosophy incredibly highly, but is, by our standards, philosophically primitive. A decent philosophy major from our world could likely out-debate the champion of theirs, just because they've deliberately frozen themselves at what they see to be perfection.</p>
<p>Incidentally, I kind of had in mind the speaker being Chancellor Anaxagoras.</p>

							</div>

								
