					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eskobar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1173523); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1173523&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608995930" alt="Eskobar" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1173523)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/eskobar" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1173523); return false;" >Eskobar</a></span> <span class="odate time_1323183424 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2011 14:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1321991">
									

<p>I'm actually sort of glad I created the University if only because it leads to stuff like this. I'm sort of shit with tales, so I'm glad someone who's a better writer found some interest in the topic.</p>
<p>You've basically gotten the same idea as I have as far as where the Universaverse (I am <em>so</em> making that a thing) is technologically: very advanced in some areas, particularly those with potential military or economic benefits (like 877 or 1080), but still lagging in areas like medicine. As far as civil rights goes, I figure the ruling class in this world believes itself to be the direct descendant of the ideas laid out in Plato's <em>Republic</em>: philosopher-kings making laws, heavily-armed soldiers enforcing laws, and everyone else doing what they're told. They don't understand just how far they've fallen morally, which is why when they're faced with something that challenges their interpretations of themselves (like SCP-1083), they send it back for repairs.</p>
<p>Anyway, this is fucking awesome, Anax, and I would say that even if it weren't mah baybee.</p>

							</div>

								
					
